{"answer": "{
  "summary": "Bounded, additive C++ fixture proposal for the §54 cross-page A destination experiment, applied to the isolated stage-54 out/shared-read-permission-frontier-20261009/multi_test.cpp. Two new file-scope option statics (+a-dst-offset=0|3072, +a-next-pte-delay=N) and three Tb run-state members are added; run_natural() gains a separate nat_a_dst_off so the shared V destination stays at offset 0 while the A destination may move to 3072 (2048-byte A copy then spans PA 0x90100c00..0x901013ff, i.e. A dst page 0 last 1 KiB + page 1 first 1 KiB). The verification loop is split so V and A use their own offsets; all first+second A destination pages are still checked byte-for-byte with every byte outside the written interval required to keep its pre-copy value. The bounded next-page-PTE delay is injected only into the ONE DDR walker read whose byte range covers the ACTUAL A destination second-page leaf PTE (derived as 0x70000 + 9*8 = 0x70048, never hardcoded unverified), by adding N to that single mem_q latency, so only that request's first RVALID is stretched and no other A context/source traffic is touched. All existing ordinary/shared strict checks (per-flow 256 physical W, source R classification, once-job issue/done, AXI held-VALID stability shadows) are preserved unchanged. End JSON is extended with a_dst_offset / a_next_pte_delay / a_next_pte_delay_applied / a_next_pte_ar_matches / a_next_pte_addr, and a hard CHECK makes a silently-ignored +a-next-pte-delay fail. The hardware-legalizer 4 KiB W-split cannot be derived from the isolated stage-53 files (critical RTL not implemented yet); necessary root read files are marked instead of asserting the split. No RTL is drafted, no memory-interleave proposal is applied, and high/max defaults keep their existing behaviour.",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "claim": "Shared mode currently forces BOTH flows' destination offset to 0, and V/A share a single nat_dst_off, so a distinct A offset does not exist today.",
      "cite": "out/shared-read-permission-frontier-20261009/multi_test.cpp:1099 (nat_dst_off = shared_source ? 0u : NAT_DST_OFF); :1100 (conf); :1180 and :1185 (both REG_DST writes use nat_dst_off); :524 (single nat_dst_off member)"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The terminal A/V destination byte check uses one off_beats for both flows; it must be split for a cross-page A destination.",
      "cite": "out/shared-read-permission-frontier-20261009/multi_test.cpp:1242-1256"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The pre-copy destination snapshot already spans NAT_DST_PAGES=9 A destination pages, i.e. it already covers the second A destination page; no snapshot-structure extension is required.",
      "cite": "out/shared-read-permission-frontier-20261009/multi_test.cpp:1073-1075, 1081-1084 (dst_words = NAT_DST_PAGES*PAGE_BEATS = 4608, nat_dst_saved[1][k] = read64(NAT_A_DST_PAGE_PA + k*8)); :115 (NAT_DST_PAGES = 9)"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The A context L0 leaf table is at PA 0x70000 and destination leaves begin at index 8; A destination page 0 leaf = 0x70040, page 1 (next page) leaf = 0x70048. L0 index of IOVA 0x20008000 is 8.",
      "cite": "out/shared-read-permission-frontier-20261009/multi_test.cpp:1035-1036 (A root 0x30000 -> L1A 0x60800 -> L0A 0x70000); :1040-1042 (dst leaf at 0x70000 + (8+i)*8)"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Derivation for the delayed address: A dst IOVA base 0x20008000 + 3072 = 0x20008c00; last copied byte = 0x20008c00 + 2048 - 1 = 0x200093ff; (0x200093ff>>12)&0x1ff = 9 => leaf 0x70000 + 9*8 = 0x70048. PHY first 1 KiB = 0x90100c00, second 1 KiB = 0x90101000.",
      "cite": "out/shared-read-permission-frontier-20261009/multi_test.cpp:112 (NAT_A_DST_PAGE_IOVA = 0x20008000); :113 (NAT_A_DST_PAGE_PA = 0x90100000); :116 (NAT_DST_OFF = 3072)"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Region classification already maps the whole 0x90100000..0x901fffff window to NR_ADST, so A physical W beats on BOTH the first and second A destination pages are counted as ADST, and source reads stay in NR_VSRC.",
      "cite": "out/shared-read-permission-frontier-20261009/multi_test.cpp:134-140 (nat_pregion: 0x90100000..0x90200000 -> NR_ADST; 0x80000000..0x80100000 -> NR_VSRC)"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Per-W-beat classification uses the pending completion AW head address, so a cross-page A write split into two AWs still classifies every beat of both pages from its own AW address.",
      "cite": "out/shared-read-permission-frontier-20261009/multi_test.cpp:2074-2083 (caw_q.front() -> nat_pregion(c.addr) -> nat_pw_beats[reg]); :2084-2097 (same-cycle accepted AW)"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The delay must be injected at the DDR AR acceptance point, where a MemRead's latency is set; drive_ddr() counts that latency down before the first RVALID, so adding N to that one entry delays only that read's first RVALID.",
      "cite": "out/shared-read-permission-frontier-20261009/multi_test.cpp:2507-2515 (f_ddr_ar -> MemRead r; r.latency = (int)ptw_latency; mem_q.push_back); :940-946 (drive_ddr latency countdown before ddr_r_valid=1)"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The walker/DDR port used by the PTW is ID slv 3 ((id>>4)&3 == 3), so the delay match can be restricted to the walker port.",
      "cite": "out/shared-read-permission-frontier-20261009/multi_test.cpp:923-928 (ds_priority rotates (id>>4)&3 == 3); :2055, :2062, :2106 (completion payload is (id>>4)&3 == 2)"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The q_write_splitter prototype does NOT perform the 4 KiB split: it REQUIRES an already aligned 2 KiB parent (aw.addr[11:0]==0, aw.len==255) and $fatals otherwise, so a raw cross-page A parent must be split UPSTREAM by the legalizer.",
      "cite": "out/shared-read-permission-frontier-20261009/q_write_splitter.sv:60-63"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The legalizer is part of the two real dma_core_wrap pipelines that produce the translation-request AW/W, i.e. the split stage lives there (source file not present in this isolated copy).",
      "cite": "out/shared-read-permission-frontier-20261009/multi_test.cpp:8-9"
    },
    {
      "claim": "shared_pretl_read only shapes READ requests, so it is NOT the module that would split the A W at 4 KiB.",
      "cite": "out/shared-read-permission-frontier-20261009/shared_pretl_read.sv:1-4, 20-24"
    }
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Only the shared-source natural 2 KiB geometry is changed by +a-dst-offset; the ordinary (non-shared) natural run keeps its existing A and V destination offset NAT_DST_OFF (3072), so ordinary behaviour is bit-identical.",
    "+a-dst-offset is accepted only as 0 or 3072 and only together with +natural=1 +shared-source=1. +a-next-pte-delay is accepted only together with +a-dst-offset=3072 (the only geometry that reaches the second A destination page).",
    "The A destination second-page leaf PTE is at PA 0x70048 and is read on the shared-DDR walker port. The delay matches by byte-range coverage of that address, so it fires whether the walker issues a single-PTE read (addr 0x70048) or a line read that covers it (e.g. addr 0x70040 len>=1); the actual read address is not asserted.",
    "The bounded delay is implemented in the Verilator memory model (testbench), i.e. as a pre-first-RVALID setup/latency stretch on that one request. If Codex root instead wants the DUT itself to hold the PTE preparation, the C++ side would only observe it; this patch does not draft that RTL.",
    "The legalizer really splits the A write at the 4 KiB boundary into two <=256-beat parents; the C++ checks depend only on total beat counts (256 physical W per flow) and not on the split count, so they are valid either way.",
    "N is bounded to 0..100000 so a single delayed read stays below WATCHDOG_CYCLES (200000) in multi_test.cpp:709, keeping the harness bounded.",
    "The existing NATURAL / PLACEMENT / SHARE50 / SHARE51 JSON schemas and all existing CHECK macros are preserved; only additive fields are introduced.",
    "No DUT was executed and no counter value is claimed as measured; all statements about hardware behaviour remain proposals pending Codex verification."
  ],
  "patches": [
    {
      "file": "out/shared-read-permission-frontier-20261009/multi_test.cpp",
      "old": "static bool task_parent_reuse_enabled = true;\nstatic bool task_parent_prepare_enabled = false;",
      "new": "static bool task_parent_reuse_enabled = true;\nstatic bool task_parent_prepare_enabled = false;\n// §54 cross-page A destination fixture (test-only, natural actual-DMA run).\n// +a-dst-offset=0|3072 (default 0): effective A-side destination offset in the\n// shared-source natural 2 KiB geometry.  3072 makes the 2048-byte A copy reach\n// the second A destination page (physical first 1 KiB at PA 0x9010_0c00,\n// second 1 KiB at PA 0x9010_1000).  The ordinary (non-shared) path keeps its\n// existing A destination offset NAT_DST_OFF (3072) and is unchanged.\n// +a-next-pte-delay=N (default 0): bounded delay inserted BEFORE the first DDR\n// RVALID of the ONE read that covers the actual A destination next-page leaf\n// PTE address; it delays no other A context/source traffic.  Both flags are\n// inert unless given.\nstatic uint32_t a_dst_offset_opt = 0;   // +a-dst-offset (0|3072)\nstatic uint32_t a_next_pte_delay = 0;   // +a-next-pte-delay (0..100000)"
    },
    {
      "file": "out/shared-read-permission-frontier-20261009/multi_test.cpp",
      "old": "static const uint32_t NAT_DST_OFF         = 3072;            // dst page offset",
      "new": "static const uint32_t NAT_DST_OFF         = 3072;            // dst page offset\n// §54 cross-page A destination fixture constants.  setup_memory_natural()\n// builds the A context L0 table at NAT_A_L0_PA and its destination leaves\n// begin at NAT_A_DST_L0_IDX; the A destination IOVA base is\n// NAT_A_DST_PAGE_IOVA (0x2000_8000).  With A destination offset 3072 over a\n// 2048-byte copy the second destination page's L0 leaf index is\n// NAT_A_DST_L0_IDX+1 (derived from the last copied IOVA byte below).\nstatic const uint64_t NAT_A_L0_PA         = 0x70000ULL;      // A L0 table base\nstatic const uint32_t NAT_A_DST_L0_IDX    = 8;               // first A dst leaf"
    },
    {
      "file": "out/shared-read-permission-frontier-20261009/multi_test.cpp",
      "old": "    // Runtime destination offset: NAT_DST_OFF (3072) normally, forced to 0 by\n    // run_natural() when shared_source is set (single 2 KiB page by default).\n    uint32_t    nat_dst_off    = NAT_DST_OFF;",
      "new": "    // Runtime destination offset: NAT_DST_OFF (3072) normally, forced to 0 by\n    // run_natural() when shared_source is set (single 2 KiB page by default).\n    uint32_t    nat_dst_off    = NAT_DST_OFF;\n    // §54 A-side destination offset, kept SEPARATE from the V/common\n    // nat_dst_off so the cross-page fixture can move A onto a second-page\n    // destination while V stays page-aligned.  Shared mode: 0 by default, 3072\n    // with +a-dst-offset=3072.  Ordinary mode: NAT_DST_OFF (3072), unchanged.\n    uint32_t    nat_a_dst_off  = NAT_DST_OFF;\n    // §54 cross-page run state (test-only).  The delay is applied at most once\n    // to the one DDR read whose byte range covers a_next_pte_addr; all three\n    // values are reported in NATURAL-JSON, so a silently ignored\n    // +a-next-pte-delay cannot pass.\n    uint32_t    a_next_pte_delay_applied = 0;  // 1 once the delay was inserted\n    uint32_t    a_next_pte_ar_matches    = 0;  // PTW ARs covering that address\n    uint64_t    a_next_pte_addr          = 0;  // actual delayed leaf PTE PA"
    },
    {
      "file": "out/shared-read-permission-frontier-20261009/multi_test.cpp",
      "old": "        // §50: shared-source mode is page-aligned (dst_offset 0, single 2 KiB\n        // page by default) and uses the CONF=129 experiment\n        // (decouple_rw | AxCACHE=0010).  The ordinary path keeps dst_offset\n        // NAT_DST_OFF (3072) and CONF=1 unchanged.\n        nat_dst_off = shared_source ? 0u : (uint32_t)NAT_DST_OFF;\n        const uint64_t conf = shared_source ? 129ULL : 1ULL;\n\n        std::printf(\"== natural write-order run: bytes=%llu beats_per_dma=%u \"\n                    \"first=%s conf=%llu shared_src=%d src_off=0 dst_off=%u ==\\n\",\n                    (unsigned long long)natural_bytes, (unsigned)beats,\n                    natural_first.c_str(), (unsigned long long)conf,\n                    (int)shared_source, (unsigned)nat_dst_off);",
      "new": "        // §50/§54: shared-source mode is page-aligned for V (dst_offset 0) and\n        // uses the CONF=129 experiment (decouple_rw | AxCACHE=0010).  The A\n        // destination offset is 0 by default and becomes +a-dst-offset (0|3072)\n        // in shared mode; 3072 makes the 2048-byte A copy reach the second A\n        // destination page.  The ordinary path keeps dst_offset NAT_DST_OFF\n        // (3072) for BOTH flows and CONF=1 unchanged.\n        nat_dst_off   = shared_source ? 0u : (uint32_t)NAT_DST_OFF;\n        nat_a_dst_off = shared_source ? a_dst_offset_opt : (uint32_t)NAT_DST_OFF;\n        const uint64_t conf = shared_source ? 129ULL : 1ULL;\n\n        // §54 actual A destination next-page leaf PTE address.  Derived from\n        // the LAST copied A destination IOVA byte, never assumed: the A L0\n        // table is at NAT_A_L0_PA and the destination leaves begin at\n        // NAT_A_DST_L0_IDX.  Inert (address 0) when the A destination stays\n        // inside its first page.\n        a_next_pte_delay_applied = 0;\n        a_next_pte_ar_matches    = 0;\n        a_next_pte_addr          = 0;\n        if (nat_a_dst_off != 0) {\n            const uint64_t last_byte =\n                NAT_A_DST_PAGE_IOVA + (uint64_t)nat_a_dst_off +\n                (uint64_t)natural_bytes - 1ULL;\n            const uint32_t l0_idx = (uint32_t)((last_byte >> 12) & 0x1FFULL);\n            CHECK(l0_idx >= NAT_A_DST_L0_IDX,\n                  \"natural(cross-page): A destination last byte precedes the \"\n                  \"A destination leaf range\");\n            CHECK(l0_idx < NAT_A_DST_L0_IDX + NAT_DST_PAGES,\n                  \"natural(cross-page): A destination second page is not \"\n                  \"mapped by setup_memory_natural(); raise NAT_DST_PAGES or \"\n                  \"add the second-page PTE\");\n            a_next_pte_addr = NAT_A_L0_PA + (uint64_t)l0_idx * 8ULL;\n        }\n\n        std::printf(\"== natural write-order run: bytes=%llu beats_per_dma=%u \"\n                    \"first=%s conf=%llu shared_src=%d src_off=0 dst_off=%u \"\n                    \"a_dst_off=%u ==\\n\",\n                    (unsigned long long)natural_bytes, (unsigned)beats,\n                    natural_first.c_str(), (unsigned long long)conf,\n                    (int)shared_source, (unsigned)nat_dst_off,\n                    (unsigned)nat_a_dst_off);\n        std::printf(\"== natural cross-page A: a_next_pte_addr=0x%016llx \"\n                    \"a_next_pte_delay=%u ==\\n\",\n                    (unsigned long long)a_next_pte_addr,\n                    (unsigned)a_next_pte_delay);"
    },
    {
      "file": "out/shared-read-permission-frontier-20261009/multi_test.cpp",
      "old": "        cfg_wr(SEL_A, REG_CONF, conf);\n        cfg_wr(SEL_A, REG_SRC,  NAT_A_SRC_IOVA);\n        cfg_wr(SEL_A, REG_DST,  NAT_A_DST_PAGE_IOVA + (uint64_t)nat_dst_off);",
      "new": "        cfg_wr(SEL_A, REG_CONF, conf);\n        cfg_wr(SEL_A, REG_SRC,  NAT_A_SRC_IOVA);\n        cfg_wr(SEL_A, REG_DST,  NAT_A_DST_PAGE_IOVA + (uint64_t)nat_a_dst_off);"
    },
    {
      "file": "out/shared-read-permission-frontier-20261009/multi_test.cpp",
      "old": "        const uint32_t off_beats = nat_dst_off / 8;              // 384 ordinary, 0 shared\n        const uint32_t dst_beats = NAT_DST_PAGES * PAGE_BEATS;   // 4608\n        for (uint32_t k = 0; k < dst_beats; ++k) {\n            const bool copied = (k >= off_beats) && (k < off_beats + beats);\n            const uint64_t want_v = copied ? nat_src_saved[0][k - off_beats]\n                                           : nat_dst_saved[0][k];\n            const uint64_t want_a = copied ? nat_src_saved[1][k - off_beats]\n                                           : nat_dst_saved[1][k];\n            CHECK(read64(NAT_V_DST_PAGE_PA + (uint64_t)k * 8) == want_v,\n                  \"natural: V destination bytes differ from the copied source \"\n                  \"(untouched head/tail must keep their pre-copy value)\");\n            CHECK(read64(NAT_A_DST_PAGE_PA + (uint64_t)k * 8) == want_a,\n                  \"natural: A destination bytes differ from the copied source \"\n                  \"(untouched head/tail must keep their pre-copy value)\");\n        }",
      "new": "        const uint32_t dst_beats = NAT_DST_PAGES * PAGE_BEATS;   // 4608\n        // V/common destination uses nat_dst_off; §54 A destination uses its own\n        // offset, so the cross-page fixture spans the first and second A\n        // destination pages while V stays page-aligned.\n        const uint32_t off_beats   = nat_dst_off / 8;    // 384 ordinary, 0 shared\n        const uint32_t off_beats_a = nat_a_dst_off / 8;  // 384 both modes\n        for (uint32_t k = 0; k < dst_beats; ++k) {\n            const bool copied_v = (k >= off_beats) && (k < off_beats + beats);\n            const bool copied_a = (k >= off_beats_a) &&\n                                  (k < off_beats_a + beats);\n            const uint64_t want_v = copied_v ? nat_src_saved[0][k - off_beats]\n                                             : nat_dst_saved[0][k];\n            const uint64_t want_a = copied_a ? nat_src_saved[1][k - off_beats_a]\n                                             : nat_dst_saved[1][k];\n            CHECK(read64(NAT_V_DST_PAGE_PA + (uint64_t)k * 8) == want_v,\n                  \"natural: V destination bytes differ from the copied source \"\n                  \"(untouched head/tail must keep their pre-copy value)\");\n            CHECK(read64(NAT_A_DST_PAGE_PA + (uint64_t)k * 8) == want_a,\n                  \"natural: A destination bytes differ from the copied source \"\n                  \"(untouched head/tail must keep their pre-copy value)\");\n        }\n        // §54 explicit cross-page certificate: the A destination interval\n        // really covers the second A destination page, so BOTH A destination\n        // pages are proven byte-for-byte.  For off_beats_a=384, beats=256:\n        // first page k=0..383 and second page k=640..1023 must keep their\n        // pre-copy value, k=384..639 must carry the copied payload.\n        if (nat_a_dst_off != 0) {\n            CHECK(off_beats_a < PAGE_BEATS,\n                  \"natural(cross-page): A destination starts past the first A \"\n                  \"destination page\");\n            CHECK(off_beats_a + beats > PAGE_BEATS,\n                  \"natural(cross-page): A destination does not reach the \"\n                  \"second A destination page\");\n            CHECK(off_beats_a + beats <= dst_beats,\n                  \"natural(cross-page): A destination leaves the mapped A \"\n                  \"destination pages\");\n        }"
    },
    {
      "file": "out/shared-read-permission-frontier-20261009/multi_test.cpp",
      "old": "        CHECK(nat_hw_a_issue_cycle >= 0 && nat_hw_a_done_cycle >= 0 &&\n              nat_hw_a_done_cycle > nat_hw_a_issue_cycle,\n              \"natural: hardware A done cycle is not after issue cycle\");",
      "new": "        CHECK(nat_hw_a_issue_cycle >= 0 && nat_hw_a_done_cycle >= 0 &&\n              nat_hw_a_done_cycle > nat_hw_a_issue_cycle,\n              \"natural: hardware A done cycle is not after issue cycle\");\n\n        // ---- (5b) §54 cross-page A destination / PTE-delay certificate ----\n        // A requested +a-next-pte-delay must really have stretched the first\n        // RVALID of the read that covers the actual A destination next-page\n        // leaf PTE.  A silent no-op is a hard failure, so the run cannot pass\n        // while pretending the delay was applied.  This runs only after every\n        // original full-copy / hardware CHECK above has passed.\n        if (a_next_pte_delay != 0) {\n            CHECK(nat_a_dst_off != 0,\n                  \"natural(cross-page): +a-next-pte-delay needs a cross-page A \"\n                  \"destination (+a-dst-offset=3072)\");\n            CHECK(a_next_pte_addr != 0,\n                  \"natural(cross-page): A destination next-page leaf PTE was \"\n                  \"never resolved\");\n            CHECK(a_next_pte_delay_applied == 1,\n                  \"natural(cross-page): +a-next-pte-delay was requested but no \"\n                  \"walker read covered the actual A destination next-page \"\n                  \"leaf PTE\");\n        }"
    },
    {
      "file": "out/shared-read-permission-frontier-20261009/multi_test.cpp",
      "old": "            \"\\\"natural\\\":1,\\\"natural_bytes\\\":%llu,\\\"natural_first\\\":\\\"%s\\\",\\\"\"\n            \"\\\"shared_source\\\":%d,\\\"conf\\\":%d,\\\"src_offset\\\":0,\\\"dst_offset\\\":%u,\\\"\"",
      "new": "            \"\\\"natural\\\":1,\\\"natural_bytes\\\":%llu,\\\"natural_first\\\":\\\"%s\\\",\\\"\"\n            \"\\\"shared_source\\\":%d,\\\"conf\\\":%d,\\\"src_offset\\\":0,\\\"dst_offset\\\":%u,\\\"\"\n            \"\\\"a_dst_offset\\\":%u,\\\"a_next_pte_delay\\\":%u,\\\"\"\n            \"\\\"a_next_pte_delay_applied\\\":%u,\\\"a_next_pte_ar_matches\\\":%u,\\\"\"\n            \"\\\"a_next_pte_addr\\\":\\\"0x%016llx\\\",\\\"\""
    },
    {
      "file": "out/shared-read-permission-frontier-20261009/multi_test.cpp",
      "old": "            (int)shared_source, (int)(shared_source ? 129 : 1),\n            (unsigned)nat_dst_off,\n            (unsigned long long)n_nat_vaw, (unsigned long long)n_nat_var,",
      "new": "            (int)shared_source, (int)(shared_source ? 129 : 1),\n            (unsigned)nat_dst_off,\n            (unsigned)nat_a_dst_off,\n            (unsigned)a_next_pte_delay,\n            (unsigned)a_next_pte_delay_applied,\n            (unsigned)a_next_pte_ar_matches,\n            (unsigned long long)a_next_pte_addr,\n            (unsigned long long)n_nat_vaw, (unsigned long long)n_nat_var,"
    },
    {
      "file": "out/shared-read-permission-frontier-20261009/multi_test.cpp",
      "old": "        if (f_ddr_ar) {\n            ++n_ddr_ar;\n            ++n_slv_ar[(s_ddr_ar_i >> 4) & 3];\n            MemRead r; r.port = P_DDR; r.addr = s_ddr_ar_a;\n            r.len = (uint8_t)s_ddr_ar_l; r.id = (uint8_t)s_ddr_ar_i;\n            r.beat = 0; r.latency = (int)ptw_latency;\n            r.accepted_cycle = g_cycle;\n            mem_q.push_back(r);\n        }",
      "new": "        if (f_ddr_ar) {\n            ++n_ddr_ar;\n            ++n_slv_ar[(s_ddr_ar_i >> 4) & 3];\n            MemRead r; r.port = P_DDR; r.addr = s_ddr_ar_a;\n            r.len = (uint8_t)s_ddr_ar_l; r.id = (uint8_t)s_ddr_ar_i;\n            r.beat = 0; r.latency = (int)ptw_latency;\n            r.accepted_cycle = g_cycle;\n            // §54 bounded A next-page leaf PTE preparation delay.  Inserted\n            // BEFORE the first RVALID of the ONE walker read whose byte range\n            // covers a_next_pte_addr; it stretches only that request's first\n            // response and touches no other A context/source traffic.\n            if (a_next_pte_delay != 0 && a_next_pte_delay_applied == 0 &&\n                a_next_pte_addr != 0 && ((s_ddr_ar_i >> 4) & 3u) == 3u) {\n                const uint64_t lo = r.addr;\n                const uint64_t hi = r.addr + (uint64_t)(r.len + 1u) * 8ULL;\n                if (lo <= a_next_pte_addr && a_next_pte_addr < hi) {\n                    r.latency += (int)a_next_pte_delay;\n                    a_next_pte_delay_applied = 1;\n                }\n                ++a_next_pte_ar_matches;\n            }\n            mem_q.push_back(r);\n        }"
    },
    {
